<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victor Emmanuel I of Sardinia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1759">1759</a>–<a href="/years/1824">1824</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Victor Emmanuel I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victor Emmanuel I was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from 1802 to 1821. While the French held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> he lived on the island of Sardinia, and in 1814 he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, where he restored the old order and in 1815 gained the former Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>. In 1814 he founded the Carabinieri. After a liberal military revolt in 1821 he abdicated in favour of his brother Charles Felix.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-i-of-sardinia.jpg" alt="Victor Emmanuel I of Sardinia" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luigi Bernero · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_du_Roi_Vittorio_Emanuele_I_di_Savoia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
